rse means creating  opportunities for communication  communication being the big deal you  have to talk to your users to understand  what they genuinely need we hosted an  open science unconference locally and  had faculty attend and kind of talk to  us about what open science meant to them  practically and then conducted formal  informal follow-up interviews with  anybody who expressed interest in the  unconference essentially and we kind of  found two major issues that were  universal across the board would anybody  we talk to there's a perceived modern  research skills gap there's a sense that  there are skills out there that you need  as a researcher that intersect with your  work in some way would enable modes of  work that you're not engaged with yet  but you don't quite know how to pick  them up or which direction to go in  first and there's there insufficient  incentives overall to enable that the  level of exploration needed to kind of  figure out which skill set is the best  for you and so we started off with a  right off the bat trying to address this  modern research skills gap through the  summer of open science over the past  summer we held a series of ten workshops  five per summer term at our institution  designed to address some of the biggest  tools and topics that came out of this  user research and this is kind of a  general idea of our promotion we we  really shared collective knowledge  within the libraries to develop this  series and to to kind of get the content  out there this is representative of our  team all of whom come from different  departments within the libraries and it  was a series of workshops and events  around scientific computing with Python  understanding your scholarly identity as  well as a series of meetups which kind  of continued the sense of  munication and enabled community  building which we had which was one of  the goals of the initiative and this is  an example of our impact this is a  Python and scientific computi